  "question": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> gas adsorbs on charcoal following Freundlich adsorption isotherm. For a given amount of charcoal, the mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> adsorbed becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>64</mn></math> times when the pressure of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is doubled.</p><p>The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> in the Freundlich isotherm equation is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;(Round off to the Nearest Integer)</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "17",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Freundlich isotherm. ;<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mfrac></msup></math><br />Substituting values ; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mfrac><mn>64</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mfrac></msup><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>166</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8773;</mo><mn>17</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>",
